/bin/
*.test
*.out
.env
.env.local
coverage.*

# `go build ./examples/<name>/...` run from the repo root writes a binary
# named after the package here when the pattern matches exactly one main
# package — these are build artifacts of the example services, not
# anything to commit.
/heroes
/villains
/gencerts

# Tilt's local_resource build output (see examples/Tiltfile, docs/tilt-dev.md).
/examples/deploy/tilt/bin/

# Dev certs from `go run ./deploy/mtls/gencerts` (see docs/grpc.md's mTLS
# section) — generated locally, never committed.
/deploy/mtls/certs/

# `mkdocs build` output (docs.yml rebuilds this in CI; see mkdocs.yml).
/site/
